/-!
# The projectivized normal cone is the exceptional divisor of an affine blowup

Let `I` be an ideal of a commutative ring `R`. The file
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Blowup/ProjectivizedNormalConeClosedImmersion.lean` builds the
closed immersion `Stacks.Blowup.projectivizedNormalConeToBlowUpSpec` of the projectivized normal
cone `Proj (Gr_I(R)) = Proj (⨁ₙ Iⁿ/Iⁿ⁺¹)` into the blowup `Proj (⨁ₙ Iⁿ)` of `Spec R` in `I`, and
shows it lies over the closed subscheme `V(I)`. That leaves open which closed subscheme of the
blowup it is. This file answers that: it is the exceptional divisor, the closed subscheme cut out
by the inverse image `I·𝒪` of the centre.

The comparison is chartwise, over the standard opens `D₊(b⁽¹⁾)` for `b ∈ I`, which cover the
blowup. On such a chart both ideals are principal, generated by the image of `b`:

* the inverse image of the centre is, by `Stacks.Blowup.map_ideal_chartAwayMap` — this is the
  statement that `I` becomes principal on the affine blowup algebra `R[I/b]`;
* the kernel of the reduction is, because a fraction `a/b⁽¹⁾ⁿ` with `a` homogeneous of degree `n`
  dies in `Gr_I(R)` exactly when the coefficient of `a` lies in `Iⁿ⁺¹`
  (`Stacks.Blowup.reesToAssociatedGraded_eq_zero_iff_of_mem`), and such a fraction is `b` times
  the fraction whose numerator is that coefficient placed in degree `n + 1`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Blowup.ker_awayMap_reesGradedToAssociatedGraded`: **the chart identity.** On the chart
  `D₊(b⁽¹⁾)` the kernel of the reduction to the associated graded ring is the principal ideal
  generated by the image of `b`.
* `Stacks.Blowup.appLE_toSpec_basicOpen_reesDegOne`: the blowup morphism, read on sections over
  the chart `D₊(b⁽¹⁾)`, is `Stacks.Blowup.chartAwayMap` — the structure map `R ⟶ R[I/b]` of the
  chart — through the two canonical identifications.
* `Stacks.Blowup.ker_projectivizedNormalConeToBlowUpSpec`: **the projectivized normal cone is the
  exceptional divisor.** The closed immersion of the projectivized normal cone into the blowup
  cuts out the inverse image of the centre.
* `Stacks.Blowup.isPullback_projectivizedNormalConeToBlowUpSpec`: **the cartesian square.**
  `Proj (Gr_I(R))` is the fibre product of `Bl_I (Spec R)` with `Spec (R/I)` over `Spec R`.

## This is the affine case of clause (6) of Stacks tag 0FBG, and carries no attribute

Clause (6) of [Stacks, Tag 0FBG] reads `X' ∩ E = Proj_Z(C_{Z/X,*})` for a closed subscheme `Z` of
an arbitrary scheme `X`, with `X'` the blowup of `X` in `Z` sitting inside the blowup `W` of
`P¹_X` in `∞(Z)` and `E ⊆ W` the exceptional divisor of the latter. Clause (3) of the same tag,
which is registered in `StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Chow/InfinityCentreBlowup.lean`, identifies
`X' ∩ E` with the exceptional divisor of `X' ⟶ X`, so clause (6) says that the exceptional divisor
of the blowup of `X` in `Z` is the projectivized normal cone. That is what is proved here, for
`X = Spec R` affine and `Z = V(I)`.

No `@[stacks 0FBG]` attribute is attached here, because the affineness of the base is a
hypothesis the source does not make. The statement for an arbitrary scheme is
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.exceptionalDivisorIsoProjectivizedNormalCone`, proved by relative-`Proj`
base change along the closed immersion of the centre, and clause (6) itself is
`Stacks.Chow.strictTransformOnExceptionalIsoProjectivizedNormalCone`, where the tag is registered.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0FBG](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0FBG)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0630](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0630)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory CommRingCat HomogeneousLocalization Polynomial

universe u

namespace Stacks.Blowup


variable {R : Type u} [CommRing R] (I : Ideal R)

/-! ### Homogeneous elements of the Rees algebra on a chart -/

/-- A power of `b⁽¹⁾` times a homogeneous element of degree `n` is homogeneous of degree
`k + n`. -/
theorem reesDegOne_pow_mul_mem {b : R} (hb : b ∈ I) (k n : ℕ) {a : reesAlgebra I}
    (ha : a ∈ reesGrading I n) :
    reesDegOne I hb ^ k * a ∈ reesGrading I (k + n) :=
  SetLike.mul_mem_graded
    (by simpa using SetLike.pow_mem_graded k (reesDegOne_mem_reesGrading I hb)) ha

/-- **A homogeneous fraction whose numerator has coefficient in `Iᵐ⁺¹` is `b` times another
fraction on the chart `D₊(b⁽¹⁾)`.** This is the one computation behind the chart identity: the
witness is the fraction whose numerator is that coefficient placed in degree `m + 1`. -/
theorem awayMk_eq_chartAwayMap_mul {b : R} (hb : b ∈ I) {m : ℕ} {c : reesAlgebra I}
    (hc : c ∈ reesGrading I (m • 1)) {γ : R} (hγ : γ ∈ I ^ (m + 1))
    (hcγ : ((c : R[X])) = monomial m γ)
    (hd : ((reesGradingEquivPow I (m + 1) ⟨γ, hγ⟩ : reesGrading I (m + 1)) : reesAlgebra I)
      ∈ reesGrading I ((m + 1) • 1)) :
    Away.mk (reesGrading I) (reesDegOne_mem_reesGrading I hb) m c hc
      = chartAwayMap I hb b *
        Away.mk (reesGrading I) (reesDegOne_mem_reesGrading I hb) (m + 1)
          ((reesGradingEquivPow I (m + 1) ⟨γ, hγ⟩ : reesGrading I (m + 1)) : reesAlgebra I) hd := by
  have key : (1 * reesDegOne I hb ^ (m + 1)) * c
      = reesDegOne I hb ^ m *
        (((reesGradingZeroEquiv I b : reesGrading I 0) : reesAlgebra I) *
          ((reesGradingEquivPow I (m + 1) ⟨γ, hγ⟩ : reesGrading I (m + 1)) : reesAlgebra I)) := by
    refine Subtype.ext ?_
    simp only [Subalgebra.coe_mul, one_mul, SubmonoidClass.coe_pow,
      coe_reesDegOne, coe_coe_reesGradingZeroEquiv, coe_reesGradingEquivPow, hcγ, monomial_pow,
      C_mul_monomial, monomial_mul_monomial]
    rw [show m + 1 + m = m + (m + 1) by omega]
    exact congrArg (monomial (m + (m + 1))) (by ring)
  apply HomogeneousLocalization.val_injective
  rw [HomogeneousLocalization.val_mul, chartAwayMap_val, Away.val_mk, Away.val_mk,
    Localization.mk_mul, Localization.mk_eq_mk_iff]
  exact Localization.r_of_eq key

/-! ### The kernel of the reduction on a chart -/

/-- **The kernel of the reduction to the associated graded ring, on the chart `D₊(b⁽¹⁾)`.** It is
the principal ideal generated by the image of `b` under the structure map `R ⟶ R[I/b]` of the
chart.

One inclusion is the computation `Stacks.Blowup.awayMk_eq_chartAwayMap_mul`: a fraction in the
kernel can, after multiplying numerator and denominator by a power of `b⁽¹⁾`, be written with a
numerator whose coefficient lies in the next power of `I`, and such a fraction is divisible by
`b`. The other is that `b` itself dies, since the degree-zero part of the reduction is
`R ⟶ R/I`. -/
theorem ker_awayMap_reesGradedToAssociatedGraded {b : R} (hb : b ∈ I) :
    RingHom.ker (Away.map (reesGradedToAssociatedGraded I) (reesDegOne I hb))
      = Ideal.span {chartAwayMap I hb b} := by
  have hf := reesDegOne_mem_reesGrading I hb
  refine le_antisymm (fun z hz => ?_) (Ideal.span_le.mpr ?_)
  · obtain ⟨n, a, ha, rfl⟩ := Away.mk_surjective (reesGrading I) hf z
    obtain ⟨k, hk⟩ := (Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.HomogeneousAwayMap.awayMk_mem_ker_awayMap_iff
      (reesGradedToAssociatedGraded I) hf n a ha).1 hz
    have han : a ∈ reesGrading I n := by simpa using ha
    have hcm := reesDegOne_pow_mul_mem I hb k n han
    have hc : reesDegOne I hb ^ k * a ∈ reesGrading I ((k + n) • 1) := by simpa using hcm
    have hγ : (((reesDegOne I hb ^ k * a : reesAlgebra I) : R[X])).coeff (k + n)
        ∈ I ^ (k + n + 1) :=
      (reesToAssociatedGraded_eq_zero_iff_of_mem I hcm).1 hk
    have hsame : Away.mk (reesGrading I) hf n a ha
        = Away.mk (reesGrading I) hf (k + n) (reesDegOne I hb ^ k * a) hc := by
      apply HomogeneousLocalization.val_injective
      rw [Away.val_mk, Away.val_mk, Localization.mk_eq_mk_iff]
      refine Localization.r_of_eq ?_
      change reesDegOne I hb ^ (k + n) * a = reesDegOne I hb ^ n * (reesDegOne I hb ^ k * a)
      rw [pow_add]
      ring
    rw [hsame, awayMk_eq_chartAwayMap_mul I hb hc hγ (coe_eq_monomial I hcm)
      (by simp)]
    exact Ideal.mul_mem_right _ _ (Ideal.mem_span_singleton_self _)
  · rintro _ rfl
    have hb0 : ((reesGradingZeroEquiv I b : reesGrading I 0) : reesAlgebra I)
        ∈ reesGrading I (0 • 1) := by
      simp
    have hmk : chartAwayMap I hb b = Away.mk (reesGrading I) hf 0
        ((reesGradingZeroEquiv I b : reesGrading I 0) : reesAlgebra I) hb0 := by
      apply HomogeneousLocalization.val_injective
      rw [chartAwayMap_val, Away.val_mk]
      exact congrArg (Localization.mk _) (Subtype.ext (by simp))
    rw [SetLike.mem_coe, hmk]
    refine (Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.HomogeneousAwayMap.awayMk_mem_ker_awayMap_iff
      (reesGradedToAssociatedGraded I) hf 0 _ hb0).2 ⟨0, ?_⟩
    rw [pow_zero, one_mul, RingHom.mem_ker]
    change reesToAssociatedGraded I
      ((reesGradingZeroEquiv I b : reesGrading I 0) : reesAlgebra I) = 0
    refine (reesToAssociatedGraded_eq_zero_iff_of_mem I
      (reesGradingZeroEquiv I b).2).2 ?_
    rwa [coe_coe_reesGradingZeroEquiv, coeff_C_zero, pow_one]

/-! ### The blowup morphism on a chart -/

/-- The map on global sections induced by `Spec` of a ring homomorphism, in terms of the
canonical identifications `Γ(Spec A, ⊤) ≅ A`. -/
private theorem appTop_spec_map_ofHom {A B : Type u} [CommRing A] [CommRing B] (φ : A →+* B) :
    (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom φ)).appTop =
      ((Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of A)).hom ≫ CommRingCat.ofHom φ) ≫
        (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of B)).inv := by
  rw [Iso.eq_comp_inv]
  exact Scheme.ΓSpecIso_naturality _

/-- **The blowup morphism, read on sections over the chart `D₊(b⁽¹⁾)`, is the structure map
`R ⟶ R[I/b]` of the chart.** On the left is the identification of `Γ(Spec R, ⊤)` with `R`, on the
right Mathlib's identification of the chart ring with the sections of `Proj` over `D₊(b⁽¹⁾)`.

The composite of the chart inclusion with the blowup morphism is `Spec` of
`Stacks.Blowup.chartAwayMap` (`Stacks.Blowup.awayι_comp_toSpec`), and reading the chart inclusion
on sections inverts `AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.awayToSection`
(`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjChartSections.awayToSection_comp_awayι_appLE`); cancelling that
isomorphism leaves the claim. -/
theorem appLE_toSpec_basicOpen_reesDegOne {b : R} (hb : b ∈ I) :
    (toSpec I).appLE ⊤ (Proj.basicOpen (reesGrading I) (reesDegOne I hb)) le_top
      = (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of R)).hom ≫
        CommRingCat.ofHom (chartAwayMap I hb) ≫
          Proj.awayToSection (reesGrading I) (reesDegOne I hb) := by
  have hf := reesDegOne_mem_reesGrading I hb
  have hpre := Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjChartSections.awayι_preimage_basicOpen_self
    (reesGrading I) hf one_pos
  have hbridge := Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjChartSections.awayToSection_comp_awayι_appLE
    (reesGrading I) hf one_pos
  have hAiso : IsIso (Proj.awayToSection (reesGrading I) (reesDegOne I hb)) :=
    Stacks.ProjQuotientChartIdeal.isIso_awayToSection hf one_pos
  have hXiso : (awayChartι I hb).appLE
        (Proj.basicOpen (reesGrading I) (reesDegOne I hb)) ⊤ hpre.ge =
      @inv _ _ _ _ (Proj.awayToSection (reesGrading I) (reesDegOne I hb)) hAiso ≫
        (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of
          (Away (reesGrading I) (reesDegOne I hb)))).inv :=
    (@IsIso.eq_inv_comp _ _ _ _ _ _ hAiso _ _).mpr hbridge
  have hX : IsIso ((awayChartι I hb).appLE
      (Proj.basicOpen (reesGrading I) (reesDegOne I hb)) ⊤ hpre.ge) := by
    rw [hXiso]
    exact @IsIso.comp_isIso _ _ _ _ _ _ _ (@IsIso.inv_isIso _ _ _ _ _ hAiso) inferInstance
  have hcomp := Scheme.Hom.appLE_comp_appLE (awayChartι I hb) (toSpec I)
    ⊤ (Proj.basicOpen (reesGrading I) (reesDegOne I hb)) ⊤ le_top hpre.ge
  have hnat := appTop_spec_map_ofHom (chartAwayMap I hb)
  refine (cancel_mono ((awayChartι I hb).appLE
    (Proj.basicOpen (reesGrading I) (reesDegOne I hb)) ⊤ hpre.ge)).mp ?_
  have hι : awayChartι I hb ≫ toSpec I = Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (chartAwayMap I hb)) :=
    awayι_comp_toSpec I hb
  rw [hcomp, Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjChartSections.appLE_top_top, hι,
    hnat, hXiso]
  exact (whisker_eq _ (@IsIso.hom_inv_id_assoc _ _ _ _ _ hAiso _ _).symm).trans
    ((Category.assoc _ _ _).symm.trans (eq_whisker (Category.assoc _ _ _) _))

/-- `Stacks.Blowup.appLE_toSpec_basicOpen_reesDegOne` on underlying ring homomorphisms, with the
composite written as a composite of ring homomorphisms. -/
theorem hom_appLE_toSpec_basicOpen_reesDegOne {b : R} (hb : b ∈ I) :
    ((toSpec I).appLE ⊤ (Proj.basicOpen (reesGrading I) (reesDegOne I hb)) le_top).hom
      = (Proj.awayToSection (reesGrading I) (reesDegOne I hb)).hom.comp
          ((chartAwayMap I hb).comp (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of R)).hom.hom) :=
  congrArg CommRingCat.Hom.hom (appLE_toSpec_basicOpen_reesDegOne I hb)

/-- `Stacks.Blowup.appLE_toSpec_basicOpen_reesDegOne` on the image of an ideal of global
sections, as the image along each of the three factors in turn. -/
theorem map_appLE_toSpec_basicOpen_reesDegOne {b : R} (hb : b ∈ I)
    (J₀ : Ideal Γ(Spec (CommRingCat.of R), ⊤)) :
    Ideal.map ((toSpec I).appLE ⊤ (Proj.basicOpen (reesGrading I) (reesDegOne I hb)) le_top).hom
        J₀
      = Ideal.map (Proj.awayToSection (reesGrading I) (reesDegOne I hb)).hom
          (Ideal.map (chartAwayMap I hb)
            (Ideal.map (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of R)).hom.hom J₀)) :=
  (congrArg (fun φ => Ideal.map φ J₀) (hom_appLE_toSpec_basicOpen_reesDegOne I hb)).trans
    ((Ideal.map_map _ _).symm.trans (congrArg (Ideal.map _) (Ideal.map_map _ _).symm))

/-! ### The projectivized normal cone is the exceptional divisor -/

/-- **The kernel of the reduction on a chart, read on sections of the blowup.** -/
theorem ker_app_projectivizedNormalConeToBlowUpSpec {b : R} (hb : b ∈ I) :
    RingHom.ker ((projectivizedNormalConeToBlowUpSpec I).app
        (Proj.basicOpen (reesGrading I) (reesDegOne I hb))).hom
      = Ideal.map (Proj.awayToSection (reesGrading I) (reesDegOne I hb)).hom
        (Ideal.span {chartAwayMap I hb b}) := by
  have hf := reesDegOne_mem_reesGrading I hb
  have hiso : IsIso (Proj.awayToSection (reesGrading I) (reesDegOne I hb)) :=
    Stacks.ProjQuotientChartIdeal.isIso_awayToSection hf one_pos
  rw [← ker_awayMap_reesGradedToAssociatedGraded I hb]
  refine le_antisymm (fun x hx => ?_) (Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap.mpr fun z hz => ?_)
  · obtain ⟨z, rfl⟩ :=
      (ConcreteCategory.bijective_of_isIso
        (Proj.awayToSection (reesGrading I) (reesDegOne I hb))).2 x
    exact Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _
      ((Stacks.ProjQuotientChartIdeal.awayToSection_mem_ker_app_projMap_iff
        (reesGradedToAssociatedGraded I)
        (irrelevant_le_map_reesGradedToAssociatedGraded I) hf one_pos z).1 hx)
  · exact (Stacks.ProjQuotientChartIdeal.awayToSection_mem_ker_app_projMap_iff
      (reesGradedToAssociatedGraded I)
      (irrelevant_le_map_reesGradedToAssociatedGraded I) hf one_pos z).2 hz

/-- **The projectivized normal cone is the exceptional divisor of the affine blowup.** For a
quasi-coherent sheaf of ideals `J` on `Spec R` whose ideal of global sections is `I`, the closed
immersion `Proj (Gr_I(R)) ⟶ Bl_I (Spec R)` cuts out the inverse image `I·𝒪` of `J` under the
blowup morphism.

The two ideal sheaves are compared on the standard opens `D₊(b⁽¹⁾)` for `b ∈ I`, which cover the
blowup by `Stacks.Blowup.iSup_basicOpen_reesDegOne_eq_top`. On such a chart both are the image
under `AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.awayToSection` of the principal ideal generated by `b`: the kernel
by `Stacks.Blowup.ker_awayMap_reesGradedToAssociatedGraded`, and the inverse image of the centre
by `Stacks.Blowup.map_ideal_chartAwayMap`, since the blowup morphism on sections over the chart
is the structure map `R ⟶ R[I/b]`. -/
theorem ker_projectivizedNormalConeToBlowUpSpec
    (J : (Spec (CommRingCat.of R)).IdealSheafData)
    (hJ : Ideal.map (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of R)).hom.hom
      (J.ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩) = I) :
    (projectivizedNormalConeToBlowUpSpec I).ker = J.comap (toSpec I) := by
  refine Scheme.IdealSheafData.ext_of_iSup_eq_top
    (fun b : I => (⟨Proj.basicOpen (reesGrading I) (reesDegOne I b.2),
      Proj.isAffineOpen_basicOpen (reesGrading I) (reesDegOne I b.2)
        (reesDegOne_mem_reesGrading I b.2) one_pos⟩ : (blowUpSpec I).affineOpens))
    (iSup_basicOpen_reesDegOne_eq_top I) fun b => ?_
  rw [Scheme.Hom.ker_apply, ker_app_projectivizedNormalConeToBlowUpSpec I b.2,
    Stacks.IdealSheaf.ideal_comap_appLE J (toSpec I) ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩ _ le_top,
    map_appLE_toSpec_basicOpen_reesDegOne I b.2, hJ, map_ideal_chartAwayMap]

/-- The ideal sheaf of the closed immersion `Spec (R/I) ⟶ Spec R` has `I` for its ideal of
global sections. -/
theorem map_ideal_ker_specMap_quotientMk :
    Ideal.map (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of R)).hom.hom
        ((Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (Ideal.Quotient.mk I))).ker.ideal
          ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩) = I := by
  have hnat := appTop_spec_map_ofHom (Ideal.Quotient.mk I)
  have hker : RingHom.ker (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (Ideal.Quotient.mk I))).appTop.hom
      = Ideal.comap (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of R)).hom.hom I := by
    rw [hnat, CommRingCat.hom_comp, CommRingCat.hom_comp, CommRingCat.hom_ofHom,
      RingHom.ker_comp_of_injective _
        ((ConcreteCategory.bijective_of_isIso
          (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of (R ⧸ I))).inv).1),
      ← RingHom.comap_ker, Ideal.mk_ker]
  have hKtop : (Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop
      (RingHom.ker (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (Ideal.Quotient.mk I))).appTop.hom)).ideal
        ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top (Spec (CommRingCat.of R))⟩ =
      RingHom.ker (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (Ideal.Quotient.mk I))).appTop.hom := by
    rw [Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop_ideal,
      show (homOfLE (le_top (a := (⊤ : (Spec (CommRingCat.of R)).Opens)))) = 𝟙 _ from rfl]
    simp
  rw [Scheme.ker_of_isAffine, hKtop, hker]
  exact Ideal.map_comap_of_surjective _
    (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of R)).commRingCatIsoToRingEquiv.surjective I

/-- **The projectivized normal cone of `V(I)` in `Spec R` is the fibre product of the blowup with
`Spec (R/I)` over `Spec R`.** This is the affine case of clause (6) of [Stacks, Tag 0FBG], read
together with clause (3) of the same tag: the exceptional divisor of the blowup of `Spec R` in
`I` is `Proj (Gr_I(R))`.

The square commutes by `Stacks.Blowup.projectivizedNormalConeToBlowUpSpec_toSpec`, and
`AlgebraicGeometry.isPullback_of_isClosedImmersion` reduces cartesianness to the identity of
ideal sheaves `Stacks.Blowup.ker_projectivizedNormalConeToBlowUpSpec`. -/
@[ega "IV 19.4.2" "special case", sga "6 VII 3.7" "special case"]
theorem isPullback_projectivizedNormalConeToBlowUpSpec :
    IsPullback (projectivizedNormalConeToBlowUpSpec I)
      (AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.toSpecZero (AssociatedGraded.grading I) ≫
        Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (AssociatedGraded.gradeZeroEquiv I).toRingHom))
      (toSpec I) (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (Ideal.Quotient.mk I))) := by
  have : IsClosedImmersion (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (Ideal.Quotient.mk I))) :=
    IsClosedImmersion.spec_of_surjective _ Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective
  exact AlgebraicGeometry.isPullback_of_isClosedImmersion _ _ _ _
    ((projectivizedNormalConeToBlowUpSpec_toSpec I).trans (Category.assoc _ _ _).symm)
    (ker_projectivizedNormalConeToBlowUpSpec I _ (map_ideal_ker_specMap_quotientMk I)).symm

end Stacks.Blowup

end
